  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Kazakhstan 2024 Floodings</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Early April 2024, large floodings have taken place in both the Russian Federation and downstream Kazakhstan. More than 110,000 people have been forced to evacuate in Kazakhstan and the Russian Federation after fast-melting snow swelled the Ural River, Europe&apos;s third-longest, causing it to burst its banks and flood cities and towns along its path.According to the Ministry for Emergency Situations in Kazakhstan, more than 97,000 people were evacuated in Kazakhstan alone, while at least 12,000 people have been moved to safety in the Russian Federation, mainly from the worst-hit Orenburg region.The government of the Netherlands has been asked to support the government of Kazakhstan in their response.</narrative>
  </description>
